of interspersed dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue  with focal cystic areas  These cystic areas range from REMOVED_DATE  0 3cm in diameter with surrounding yellowish discoloration  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The axillary fat on dissection reveals multiple lymph nodes  ranging from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the upper portion of the left breast  submitted from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   No tissue submitted  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  intact  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm area  upper outer quadrant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections from the upper portion of the left breast  Received in formalin  labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm aggregate of multiple portions of tan yellow  lymph node bearing fat  which contains multiple possible lymph nodes  ranging from 0 5cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  bisected  1 inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 52 53PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVE