A IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  6  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  14  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   3  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   3  Extracapsular extension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  There is granulation tissue and fibrosis present in lymph nodes involved with tumor  The presence of isolated tumor cells in some lymph nodes  may reflect regression from a larger focus of metastatic carcinoma following neoadjuvant therapy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Meagher  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a localization wire in place  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm gray white stellate scar with central hemorrhage and an eccentric 0 8cm cavity  consistent with a previous biopsy site  The cavity comes to 0 2cm of the anterior margin  0 8cm of the superior margin  1 1cm of the posterior margin  2 0cm of the inferior margin  2 3cm of the medial margin  and 2 0cm of the lateral margin  The gray white stellate fibrous area comes to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  0 7cm of the of the superior margin  0 8cm of the anterior margin  1 5cm of the inferior margin  1 3cm of the medial margin  and 1 6cm of the lateral margin  A single silver metal clip is noted within the specimen  No secondary clip is grossly appreciated  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire gray white  stellate area  with tissue containing a silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end margin  enface  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin and labeled  left axillary contents   are 2 fragments of fatty tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  On dissection  several tan pink and tan gray lymph nodes are identified measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The larger lymph nodes are serially sectioned or bisected  A few lymph nodes show partial replacement by fatty tissue  All the lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph nodes  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Next 4 larger lymph nodes  each bisected and submitted entirely  1 lymph node per each cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller 9 candidate lymph nodes  submitted in toto  Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast final inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue  A stitch represents final margin and the stitched surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  and labeled  left breast final superior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue  A stitch marks the final margin and the stitched surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cassette  REMOVED_A