Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 34 CLINICAL DATA  None entered                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT MASS   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  50   EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID  CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPES  50   PRESENT MULTIFOCALLY AT THE INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE   ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  3 MICROSCOPIC FOCI  NOTE  The infiltrating component measures 1 1cm in greatest dimension  histologic   The ductal carcinoma in situ is present focally within and very extensively away from the infiltrating carcinoma  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 20 51 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  yellow red and tan  fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen  which is inked and sectioned to reveal fatty tissue  with a 1 0cm focal white firm area adjacent to the inked resection margin  A piece of firm area is frozen as FX 1  representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted in A through J  with FX 1 in K  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Hugh Pollard Chandler  M D  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
