n  The breast parenchyma of the upper inner quadrant also shows another irregularly outlined tan pink firm tumor measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and located 1 2cm from the nearest anterior margin  1 2cm from the nearest posterior margin  and 1 0cm lateral to the larger tumor  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense pink white fibrous stroma which extends up to both the inked anterior and posterior resection margins and shows a few cysts measuring from REMOVED_DATE up to 0 5cm in greatest dimension  Obvious lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger tumor with nearest inked margins  approximately 11 o clock position   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller tumor  lateral to the larger tumor  approximately at 12 o clock position   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion  upper inner quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  outer quadrant  predominantly lower outer quadrant  away from all the 3 lesions  Received fresh  labeled  additional superficial margin   are multiple  irregularly outlined and unoriented fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 0 8cm  The larger fragments are bisected or serially sectioned  Obvious tumor is not identified  Submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast skin   is an irregularly outlined and unoriented fragment of tan pink skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 0 5cm  The skin surface is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned  Submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 03 07PM By his her signature 