orn  M D  Edited by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 39 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Ben Zion Pilch  M D  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY ADDENDUM    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  SARCOMATOID  SPINDLE CELL  CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  The tumor is composed of spindle shaped cells  Many of the cells have the features of myofibroblasts with intracytoplasmic filaments and dense bodies  Some cells  however  contain intracytoplasmic tonofibrils confirming their epithelial differentiation  The findings are consistent with a spindle cell carcinoma  Added by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 06    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block W   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue  which is dissected to reveal two lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 2 3cm in greatest dimension  Each lymph node is bisected and frozen entirely as frozen section  1  and now in cassette K and frozen 