Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on core biopsy  There are two tumors that have been identified  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   ALL EXAMINED RESECTION MARGINS NEGATIVE FOR IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA  SURGICAL CLEARANCE   1 CM   HEALING BIOPSY SITES  2   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 34 OF 34 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS OF THE SKIN  NOTE  Two discontiguous tumors are present  with dissimilar morphology  consistent with two primary neoplasms  The invasive lobular carcinoma is negative for E cadherin by immunohistochemistry  The invasive ductal carcinoma is graded on the basis of both the current specimen and the prior biopsy  OS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the mitotic activity is more apparent in the biopsy  Hormone receptor and Her 2 studies will be performed on both tumors  blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is a 810 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse and nipple areola complex measuring REMOVED_DATE x 8 7cm  The axillary tail composes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm portion of the main specimen  There is a brown oval lesion on the white tan skin which is 2 0cm in diameter  raised 0 2cm from the surface of the skin  The anterior portion of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior black  Two irregular  somewhat ill defined nodules are identified within the breast  each is white pink  firm  and distinct from the surrounding yellow tan breast parenchyma  The first lesion  lesion  1  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and is located at the 12 o clock position approximately 6 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is 0 5cm from the deep margin  and greater than 2 0cm from the remaining margins  The second lesion  lesion  2  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located at the 10 o clock position approximately 3 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is greater than REMOVED_DATE from all of the margins  The two lesions are separated by 5 5cm  The tissue between the 2 mass lesions is mixed firm and fatty  with no apparent tumor involvement  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of lesion  1 and underlying closest relationship to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin  closest to lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue that is somewhat firm between lesion  2 and lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from medial portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from lateral portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of skin lesion and anterior margin in underlying tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible lymph nodes with attached vessels   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible matted lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible matted lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Vessels with possible attached lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Alton Brad Farris III M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Alton Brad Farris III M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 AUG 94 at 11 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  MUCINOUS  COLLOID   CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures 6 0mm in greatest dimension and is composed entirely of mucinous carcinoma  Tumor is present at an inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with a tan firm nodule  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm extending to the inked margin  No frozen section done  The nodule is submitted in A  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in B through F  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  IRREGULAR FIRM AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  WAIT FOR THE PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
