nters are Bcl 2 negative and Bcl 6 positive   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative  but may be technically suboptimal  T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  are in a normal interfollicular distribution  The nodular meshwork of the follicular dendritic cells is  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  Ki67 shows a high proliferative rate with polarization in the reactive follicles  Kappa and lambda light chains by in situ hybridization show normal polyclonal plasma cells  Overall  the morphological and immunohistochemical findings are consistent with a reactive peritumoral process  Dr  N L  Harris reviewed the slides and concurs with the interpretation  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  BOTH INVOLVING 1 OF 4 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  SEE NOTE   2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunostains for keratin  calponin  myosin  and p63 support the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  INVOLVING 2 OF 3 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple levels examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple levels examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL NODE    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL SENTINEL NODES    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES  0 2   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The lymph nodes architecture is preserved with reactive appearing well shaped germinal centers surrounded by well defined mantle zones  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  Immunostain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  performed on the larger lymph node highlights B cell rich follicles  encompassed by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive follicular dendritic cell aggregates  The interfollicular regions are rich of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive T cells in normal distribution  Kappa and lambda light chains by in situ hybridization show polyclonal plasma cells  The morphological and immunohistochemical features of the sentinel lymph node are consistent with a reactive process  Dr  N L  Harris reviewed the slides and concurs with the interpretation  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Griffin  REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan white soft lymph node which has been previously cut and has a minimal amount of attached adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely froze