essel Invasion  Not identified   Perineural Invasion  Present   Margin of Invasive Carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma comes to 0 15cm from the  medial skin margin in one focus  The remaining skin margins and parenchymal  margins are  0 2cm away   Location of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  Within the region of the mass   Grade of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  2 to focal 3   Margin of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm  or greater   Stains for Receptors  Requested       TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2  SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES    Total Number of Positive Lymph Nodes  10  Total Number of Lymph Nodes Examined  11    Number with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0    Number with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   2    Number with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   8  Extracapsular Extension  Marked   Other Forms of Axillary Involvement  Lymphatic vessels and multifocal soft  tissue metastases              Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD         PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note       Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining o