Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 19 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma of right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 5 CM   WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  MARGINS NEGATIVE  SEE NOTE  2  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH PAGETOID SPREAD  THE INFILTRATING COMPONENT EXTENDS TO SURGICAL MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Microcalcifications are present  The infiltrating lobular carcinoma grows as several apparently discrete nodules that measure in aggregate approximately 1 2cm  This component infiltrates insidiously throughout portions of the specimen  No definite vascular invasion is identified  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 23 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of yellow breast tissue  with localization wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular firm  white lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  grossly within 1mm of an inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in G  Remainder of tissue in A F  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
